/T ("If you're watching this," the older Aiden said, "then the synchronization has already started, and there's no version of tonight where you get to choose whether this decision happens. You only get to choose how it goes." A pause, and something in his exhausted face that might have been an apology. "Three paths, Aiden. I've watched all three play out, in enough failed attempts that I've stopped counting. I won't tell you which one to take. I made that mistake once, with someone I loved, and I've regretted the arrogance of it every day since. But I'll tell you exactly what each one costs, because you deserve better than I got.")
/E ("If you're watching this," the older Aiden said, "then the synchronization has already started, and there's no version of tonight where you get to choose whether this decision happens. You only get to choose how it goes." A pause, and something in his exhausted face that might have been an apology. "Three paths, Aiden. I've watched all three play out, in enough failed attempts that I've stopped counting. I won't tell you which one to take. I made that mistake once, with someone I loved, and I've regretted the arrogance of it every day since. But I'll tell you exactly what each one costs, because you deserve better than I got.")
