/T ("The merge needs an anchor," she said. "Something real enough, specific enough, loved enough, to hold every branching version of reality together around a single center instead of letting them tear each other apart on contact. Eleven of us tried to build that anchor out of code. Out of theory. It never held." She met his eyes, and for the first time since he'd met her, on the bridge or in the archive or here, she looked afraid. "It has to be a memory, Aiden. A real one. And it has to be one you're willing to give up permanently, because the engine doesn't borrow. It keeps.")
/E ("The merge needs an anchor," she said. "Something real enough, specific enough, loved enough, to hold every branching version of reality together around a single center instead of letting them tear each other apart on contact. Eleven of us tried to build that anchor out of code. Out of theory. It never held." She met his eyes, and for the first time since he'd met her, on the bridge or in the archive or here, she looked afraid. "It has to be a memory, Aiden. A real one. And it has to be one you're willing to give up permanently, because the engine doesn't borrow. It keeps.")
/Pg 177 0 R
/K [2]
>>
